<title>POLAND: Polish shares end lower in continuous trade.</title>
<headline>Polish shares end lower in continuous trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stalexport and Universal fell while Budimex rose in a 1.5-million-zloty turnover in Warsaw continuous trade on Thursday.</p>
<p>The remaining seven stocks were untraded.</p>
<p>NFI units fell in a 10.7-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
